# Copy to .env for local use, or set these in the host's build environment.

# Controls whether the build is indexable by search engines.
#
#   production  -> no robots meta tag, robots.txt allows crawling
#   anything else (including unset) -> noindex,nofollow on every page and
#                                      robots.txt disallows crawling
#
# This fails closed on purpose: staging must never be indexed. The build prints
# one line saying which mode it produced. Check it before a production deploy.
SITE_ENV=staging

# Where the contact form's enquiries are POSTed — the Zapier catch hook that
# creates the item in TLB's Monday.com board. See MONDAY-FORM-SETUP.md.
#
#   set   -> the form submits, and shows the thank-you only on a 2xx response
#   unset -> the form still RENDERS, but refuses to submit and tells the reader
#            it is not connected, rather than faking a thank-you
#
# The build prints one [FORM] line saying which of those two it produced.
# Check it on a production deploy, next to the [SEO] line.
#
# PUBLIC_ on purpose, and honestly named: this URL is inlined into the page's
# HTML and is visible in view-source. That is fine for a catch hook — it
# receives data and hands none back. NEVER put a Monday.com API token here or
# anywhere else in this repo; the token belongs in the Zapier connection.
PUBLIC_ENQUIRY_WEBHOOK_URL=
